<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article<br />
<strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Comedy, Weirdness, short and sweet</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> The Foundation stumbles upon a small family-owned restaurant that happens to serve infallibly, undeniably good food.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> After being flagged by CHORUS, A social mapping AIC designed to detect intense spikes in mood, a small pizzeria finds itself under the attention of the Foundation. The restaurant, known as Giacomo's Pizza, makes the pretty standard claim that it serves &quot;The World's Best.&quot; The thing is, for this bistro, that might actually be true. Anyone who tries Giacomo's pies agrees that they're the best they ever tasted -or will taste- to the point of profound satisfaction. The thing is, the foundation can't figure out why. It's just normal pizza; nothing memetic, nothing thaumaturgic, nothing chemical. In the end, when the lead researcher breaks down to the current Giacomo in charge, tearfully asking them what's so special about their pizza they merely reply &quot;Simple. They're made with love.&quot;<br />
<strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The hook of the article lies in the surrealist concept of an item of food being objectively &quot;the best.&quot; As well as the intrigue of the eyecatching associated image:</p>
